#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:20
#: 210c4e54a1b64d97a9732c1df83f1c4f
msgid "**Hopefully I can help somebody out and save them a lot of frustration by logging my whole build.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:24
#: 55a35cac371d4d21b91334946985b4a0
msgid "The Equipment List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:26
#: f0132b5b05e04208b63ca80b3c7bfa43
msgid "`Bixler 1.1 ARF <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/h-king-bixler-1-1-epo-1400mm-glider-arf.html>`__ (HobbyKing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:28
#: c1f0ff56b0f14d77a4788fb04d1f2627
msgid "`Motor <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-multistar-2216-800kv-14pole-multi-rotor-outrunner-v2.html>`_ (HobbyKing) or other 2216 size 800-1000KV motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:30
#: 7fa2de70ba034e29a66ebf4a5573d1ad
msgid "`ESC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-basic-18a-v3-1-speed-controller.html>`__ (HobbyKing) or other 18-20A ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:32
#: c4a9b48f245b44abb4923ee485876d0e
msgid "`SBEC <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/turnigy-5a-8-26v-sbec-for-lipo.html>`__ (HobbyKing) - (Optional) 5A BEC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:34
#: 796bfd28124e42a7b4c3c3dd599a22be
msgid "`Motor mount <https://hobbyking.com/en_us/hobbyking-bixler-and-bixler-2-motor-mount-upgrade.html>`__   (HobbyKing) - (for spinning bigger props)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:35
#: 1b5bf9166eec45ef949a56e20f5b441d
msgid "APM 2.6 with separate GPS/compass. (see note below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:36
#: d16df7f30103484293d6e178a1de703c
msgid "Radio: Spektrum DX8 and RX or any other 5 channel or higher system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:37
#: ddb3cb7e0f1247519cc38b4b4325d873
msgid "Prop: APC 8x4E . Pusher or puller may be used since motor direction is easily changed just by swapping wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:38
#: 82fa76b16fb847a1b5ea43d027a1f699
msgid "Y-servo-cable to connect both aileron servos together to one autopilot output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:41
#: e2ebb120cf9443f598204bb593387481
msgid "This autopilot is no longer supported. See the current autopilot :ref:`list<common-autopilots>`. OmnibusF4 Pro V3 is an inexpensive alternative. Any UBLOX MN-8 class GPS works well, such as a BN-220. A compass (gps/compass combo parts are available) is not necessary for ArduPilot on planes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:44
#: 9d4d0738e78d408ca3f315cf2d390065
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:46
#: e983e989b50f44e29a875f31cc9740c4
msgid "About using an external SBEC: I chose to do this because I am an RC heli guy, and I often use servos that draw ridiculous current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:48
#: a1f99516a00040dfac262448b371ca6c
msgid "If you power the servos separately from the BEC built into the ESC, there is less chance of either one shutting down due to over-current draw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:50
#: 4c566c86c0f948c5aecd3c814d512e91
msgid "But you also add a second electronic device that can fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:51
#: 7802c383e18f45449ba2832575e4576a
msgid "When the motor is at max throttle and servos are fully deflected, such as on a windy day, the separate BEC gives you some headroom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:53
#: dfec73750d05462da8024192c37291f6
msgid "There are smaller, inexpensive BECs on the market that use up less space than what I have pictured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:55
#: 61be9d469d9d4d1eab118fd9964c2a1a
msgid "This is totally optional. The ESC's BEC will work well and reliably in this application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:58
#: 672ba24e77f34468b3007501f99eaafc
msgid "Programming the ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:60
#: 90705c8a8e454899b4fe41023e21e232
msgid "Using the ESC's setup instructions, set the ESC's low voltage cutoff to its lowest setting to allow   the autopilot battery level failsafe feature do its job. (be sure to enable it!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:61
#: 8dc51a73517440e3b451ce87d45205bc
msgid "Don't worry about motor direction; you can just switch two of the motor wires if the motor spins backwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:63
#: fea06228d6874607abf2f8c394900ff7
msgid "Follow the :ref:`ESC setup guide <common-esc-calibration>` to calibrate the ESC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:66
#: 63cea56196464b0b8133253764d1b0d4
msgid "Wiring the ESC and BEC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:68
#: 681c824bfb9d4b1eab57daf63e09e011
msgid "I chose to use EC3 connectors in my build, because all of my batteries have them. XT-60 are just fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:71
#: 426c6141d684419c930dde8e2b657a85
msgid "If you do not use an external SBEC, skip to the last step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:73
#: 57dcb446b2694fdaa180eb269655c691
msgid "Cut the center servo power lead off of the ESC's BEC at the connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:74
#: 9c12f70cab2a44969c1cfb657b6faf30
msgid "Solder the SBEC power cables along with the ESC power cables into your connector (this can be a little tricky). #. Get the solder hot in a connector and insert an ESC wire. #. Keep the connection hot and slip the BEC power wire in next to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:78
#: b010b5ac93cf419aabe0cf27f5381840
msgid "I chose to run my servos at 5V  from the SBEC. #. There is a jumper on the end of it that lets you select 5 or 6 V. #. Before you reinstall the electronics secure the jumper on the SBEC with a glob of hot glue or shoe goo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:81
#: f84020ecdadd4e54ae51771bd12c4b99
msgid "Pull the center (red) pin and wire from the ESC receiver connector. #. This disconnects the built in BEC from the ESC. You don't need it since it since we are using a separate (dedicated) BEC. #. Tuck the ESCs BEC wire away with heat shrink tubing over the end. #. You will need access to it if you need to re-program the ESC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:85
#: 30c445386b714bd1a5ef7ebf19ed74c9
msgid "Add 100mm 14 gauge motor lead extensions with 3.5mm banana plugs to make it easier to wire the Bixler's motor later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:87
#: 1ab03944f9e846cd96257dff87a51170
msgid "**Here it is ready to go:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:93
#: 7ab86f068df348739dcaff5287094178
msgid "Setting up the Autopilot, Sensors, and Optional Equipment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:95
#: 7d3efd67951545b580b482c1715696a7
msgid "The purpose of this article is to detail the aircraft build, not the APM. There are many documents in the wiki covering the APM, sensors, and tuning. `Airplane walk-through <https://ardupilot.org/plane/docs/arduplane-setup.html>`_ ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:100
#: 0a94ef2608f849e898fea95dad542a8b
msgid "Mount the autopilot and install the wiring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:102
#: cb82c2f2847544b8b24c88f63f3929b1
msgid "Make a 45 x 100 mm mounting plate for the autopilot using 5mm plywood (or plastic or fiberglass board)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:104
#: 646a45ae0cb54ffc8b2fbce5c07e7cde
msgid "Use a 1\" square of Kyosho Zeal Gel or Dubro foam under each corner of the autopilot to provide vibration suppression."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:106
#: 476c3344c01645d7b02e64d4aeef9f69
msgid "Zeal has high strength double sided adhesive, but if your pads do not, consider using \"Welders Glue\" available at Amazon or Lowes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:108
#: 038dcee1bf854cb1893b6ce0fa1922b3
msgid "Re Welder's Glue: it is contact cement. Lightly cover each surface you wish to bond and let them dry for about five minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:110
#: 79055055cb034e51ad34a64d7b42226e
msgid "Then carefully align and put the two surfaces together and for immediate bonding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:112
#: e3bac0bd50344a6e8940d4011b954fff
msgid "I will also use Welder's Glue for assembling the foam air frame and building an access door in the fuselage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:115
#: f2b5d9f7e2e04c80b9e78ca7fd5bd2d4
msgid "**The APM autopilot mounted on the plate: (Pictured are the stock cables to the GPS. I actually used longer 30cm cables)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:122
#: 6a700c30d1f84c92a5c95bc44be7f5d0
msgid "Preparing the Fuselage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:124
#: 39069ad0699c4b91bdbedd41f59bbfec
msgid "For this build, the APM is mounted inverted and we want to get it level with the fuselage (level with the line of flight)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:126
#: c24f68fb4d534e03afed54e8819377e9
msgid "You can see that the wing has a positive angle of attack when the APM is level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:128
#: 051c7bec79284ce3b2f4ee8335b419c7
msgid "If you just stick the APM to the bottom or top of the fuselage it will not be level, but this will be compensated for if you set the \"LEVEL\" position to be such that the wing has a few degrees of angle of attack when doing the :ref:`Accelerometer calibration <common-accelerometer-calibration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:130
#: 6205e14fbf4b4bcbb5cb4719b94f8f8e
msgid "I removed some of the foam below the top inside of the fuselage to get the APM level:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:137
#: 4f810d9ad207415084e6f9db97a89afe
msgid "Component Placement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:139
#: b20c624a819e43a1aa56cf60f172791f
msgid "Here is the APM set in place with some of the components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:140
#: 6429e5b8c98742a8a259469c79f90fd1
msgid "At this point you should mark where your access panel will be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:146
#: 120b6a48b0a049ec807a8c9401a01447
msgid "Trimming the Fuselage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:148
#: 2eaf59c929b24773aa046dd3471d80b4
msgid "I originally cut too much and the fuselage was really weak."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:149
#: 33274314ebfe4dd6a56fc55094e0a7e2
msgid "No problem; with some hot glue you can easily fix any boo-boos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:150
#: 7c5d12bef2c3406098c26a7892a389c3
msgid "In the picture below you want to cut the lower portion and leave the area I have labeled \"Do Not Cut\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:152
#: 388d6c7a1fd846168b1a13e7e54b70bb
msgid "You will have ample room to access the APM Inputs and Outputs, as well as the USB port and other pins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:154
#: a04bc201257f4cc197a020da571fd286
msgid "Cut straight through the foam so that the panel will open easily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:159
#: 4f11ec4ccb544b29bf28216cb6bb122c
msgid "Now match up the two halves to mark the cuts for the right side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:160
#: 646309df656d424fb3affdf5cb3ccf5c
msgid "Cut a larger access panel out of the other (right) half of the fuselage so you can access the USB port on the APM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:166
#: 1f7bb7e0cde341fd9ee7d3a902a9e96c
msgid "Cut a bevel along the long axis of the large panel we already cut out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:168
#: 1ed366b62e3a4512affefaa407fa8878
msgid "I think that my picture is incorrect below; make this cut on the panel from the \\ **right half of the fuselage**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:170
#: c3750f42888c4900906083c10bbc666b
msgid "This is not the edge where the two halves of the fuselage join, but the cut near the wing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:176
#: 9d7a5c544a634b258c422f1b694a73e2
msgid "Now, make a Welder's glue hinge where the bevel (that we just cut) meets the fuselage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:178
#: ef84251b0b614074af083a57361023a1
msgid "This creates a hinge for the panel that is invisible and super cool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:179
#: c6ec77ad1f79443b8f7f042fb344d383
msgid "Don't worry, custom foamies use this type of hinge for hundreds of flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:181
#: 0ab485dc8977464295cc0e7dba83f1dc
msgid "Here is a `link <http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S-8PGFJqqMM>`_ to a YouTube video explaining how to make a Welder's hinge:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:182
#: 09ec528d94514ced961a1a1f176aa60d
msgid "The panel should look like this when the Welder's hinge is complete:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:188
#: 06fb276ccef64c508091e9b4fecdaf50
msgid "Assemble the Fuselage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:190
#: 92f373e27d24434ca12b53be26ab9608
msgid "So now I am going to fast forward a little bit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:191
#: 7ecef678114147209762bcdca5736c82
msgid "Follow the Bixler instructions and glue the halves of the fuselage together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:193
#: 23853558a4d5498a92b8d487b591d426
msgid "Again, I use Welder's glue, applying a thin bead to each half, letting them get tacky, and then assembling the halves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:195
#: e67e605427474d979ab3a88de3aa68a2
msgid "Run the motor cables from the ESC to the motor before you assemble the two halves."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:197
#: f3066a3e63e1489997caa5c52aab73a0
msgid "No worries if you don't, but it will save you the trouble of trying to attach the motor leads with needle nose pliers and hemostats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:199
#: a4f97252319b4b7eb7a703f9a48b4678
msgid "You should also check the rotation of the motor so that you do not have to switch motor leads for a motor spinning in reverse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:203
#: 6a6ec68cb5e24e588ed4d6a12e99cf29
msgid "COMPONENT Installation Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:205
#: 4653845b4f0e4549970baf688fe86bd5
msgid "Below I have the fuselage glued together and the components glued in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:207
#: 994d115639af438ea726996b69fab1c0
msgid "I like hot glue for this detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:208
#: 547652b51dde4d669229e5ca5b8d09c4
msgid "Notice that I glued a 3mm carbon fiber rod across the access hatch for added rigidity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:214
#: 98cbfca280cd4f7cab54729735c0ec73
msgid "At this point, space is becoming a concern. Using a smaller BEC will help you out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:216
#: 66dd93095e3c4ef28ea59233d7ec090e
msgid "You will notice that we have put nothing in the nose so far, and all of our components are pretty tightly tucked under the wing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:218
#: a3723b85471f491aa4e68c62e0349d1b
msgid "I did this so that we can utilize bigger batteries in future builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:219
#: 36e9eaa7b3724fbbaa887640fd8f5a60
msgid "This time around I am using an airspeed sensor which is recommended, but not necessary if you are on a first-time build budget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:221
#: bebc4b0daa0142fb87be05232df9d136
msgid "To make space for batteries, I mounted the airspeed sensor board and receiver to the bottom of the canopy hatch:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:228
#: 67c9a34327744c5582a058e7f4e3231f
msgid "Complete The Construction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:230
#: b3d46e2f15024d18980754026738112c
msgid "Use a Y servo splitter cable for the ailerons, although using separate autopilot outputs would allow the use of :ref:`flaperons<flaperons-on-plane>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:231
#: aadb12d0cd674101bb1c86dbe16fcf22
msgid "I am quite happy with this setup because you can get the CG perfect with Zippy 3s 2200mAh Lipo batteries. I was able to use up to 3000 mAh batts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:233
#: 2d1e2f31357c45e384d6cbc954c706c2
msgid "I mounted the GPS/Compass on the right wing after removing just a small amount of material."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:235
#: 23ccca87ed98433d8e394eead1e62e9d
msgid "Having it sitting up high on the wing is not ideal, but I wanted to get it away from the fuselage and all of the current-carrying electronics. I ultimately ran the cables under the wing along the carbon fiber rod, which is much smoother. If you do not use a compass, the gps can be mounted anywhere as long as its upper surface (antenna) faces the sky."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:242
#: 054f7e8152d54488bc333035d06087f5
msgid "Tuning and Flight Performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:244
#: 523edd7e95b1445190098d2e7a141af1
msgid "To get the best motor and propeller for my build, I used `eCalc <http://ecalc.ch>`__ , which is worth the money. You can also use :ref:`Drive Calculator<drivecalculator-guide>`, which is free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/a-high-quality-bixler-1-1-build.rst:247
#: db5d854d269b4b79bee6dadfaabe7ded
msgid "After going through the wizard in Mission Planner, you should have a compass that points correctly, and a properly working GPS. I found that the initial settings were quite flyable, and using the Autotune to give very good results."
